# “Dev build” = updater publish

When the user says **build a dev build**, **dev build**, **ship to testers**, or
**put it on the updater**, they mean FTP-publish **`/dev/latest.json`**.
`flutter build apk` alone is not done.

Testers install from the in-app updater / [updater.javp.app/dev](https://updater.javp.app/dev/).
A local APK is only enough when they ask for **adb install**, **sideload only**,
or **don’t publish**.

On the **Windows ship host**, a Dev publish must include **Android + Windows +
Linux**. Missing `packages.windows-x64` makes Windows clients report “already
latest” even when Android moved ahead — that is a failed ship. Do **not** call
Android-only FTP “done.” Do **not** relabel an old Windows/Linux zip as the new
`+N`.

## Do this (Windows build host)

1. `python tool/bump_dev_build.py` — `+N` must exceed live
   `https://updater.javp.app/dev/latest.json` `baseVersionCode`. **Do not commit**
   the pubspec bump.
2. Clear stale `build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/*sideloadDev*` leftovers so old
   v7a/universal APKs are not uploaded under the new `+N`.
3. Start Linux early: `gh workflow run build-linux.yml --ref dev -f channel=dev`
   (wait + `gh run download` for `javp-linux-x64-dev` before the final FTP).
4. Rebuild Android **after** the bump (`sideloadDev`, `JAVP_UPDATE_CHANNEL=dev`).
5. Build Windows locally (same bump / dart-defines):
   `python tool/apply_windows_channel_icon.py --channel dev`
   `flutter build windows --release --dart-define=JAVP_DISTRIBUTION=sideload --dart-define=JAVP_UPDATE_CHANNEL=dev`
   `python tool/package_windows.py` (zip is required; installer needs Inno Setup —
   ship the zip even if ISCC is missing; restore `windows/runner/resources/app_icon.ico`
   afterward).
6. Load `.env`, then one FTP that attaches **all** artifacts for that `+N`:
   `python tool/deploy_update.py --channel dev --apk-dir build/app/outputs/flutter-apk --skip-universal --windows-zip build/windows-dist/javp-windows-x64.zip [--windows-installer …] --linux-zip path/to/javp-linux-x64.zip`
7. Confirm `https://updater.javp.app/dev/latest.json` shows the new
   `baseVersionCode` and `packages` has **both** `windows-x64` and `linux-x64`
   (plus `apks`).

Prefer `tool/local_release.sh --channel dev` when bash + Linux zip are available.
Full hybrid: [`docs/updates.md`](docs/updates.md).

`--skip-windows` / Android-only publish is only for hosts that **cannot** build
Windows (Linux bot / Cloud), and only when the user explicitly accepts desktop
out of date.

## Do not

- Stop after a local APK unless they say **adb install**, **sideload only**, or
  **don’t publish**.
- Re-upload leftover APKs or old Windows/Linux zips as the new `+N` (wrong
  binary / updater loops). Android-only publish **drops** `packages.*` — omit
  desktop rather than relabeling `+65` zips as `+66`.
- Commit/push the Dev `+N` bump (live `latest.json` is the floor).
- Dispatch `build-windows.yml` / `build-macos.yml` / `deploy-update.yml` just to
  check a PR or get a signed APK this host can already produce.
